I simply couldn't let this rubbish pass without comment...

I play xconq on the Sun, and have some experience with the VAXStation
version.  It is a superior programme, and obviously was a MAJOR undertaking 
on the part of the author.  Furthermore, a coworker here has been dealing with
the author and found him quite willing to work on fixing bugs.  The author
further is VERY candid about the fact that there are still many bugs to be
fixed and that the vt100 stuff is of questionable utility.  It was after all
written for X Windows...

If you feel so grand as to be able to make such petty statements about the 
programme, then why don't you put youre money where youre mouth is and 
fix what you dont like.  But then, silly me, you did state that you felt it
was a waste of time.  Fine...delete it all from your machine and dont play
it.  Unless you have something to contribute, don't waste our time with your
petty diatribes...

That is not to say that we should ignore bugs and worship programme authors
regardless of the quality of thier work.  On the contrary, that is what 
this group is for.  But we should be working on fixes, not idiotic flames.
For myself, i intend to do what i can to perfect the game.  In concept and
excecution, it has many virtues, and im sure it will sap a huge amount of time
away from my other responsibilities...;'}

Oh, and one parting word:  I myself would be proud to have my name associated
with xconq.  I would not, however, want my name associated with the article 
you posted.  It shows lack of maturity and civility....    


